WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
A clear morning over Northern Ireland.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.450
By afternoon, towering
clouds bring showers.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.070
On another day, a grey sheet of
cloud rolls in from the Atlantic.

4
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.070
On a third, cloud sits
on the Mourne Mountains.

5
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.330
Some places here get about 2,000
millimetres of rain a year.

6
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.630
Others, just under 800.

7
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.470
Yet air holds its water
as an invisible gas.

8
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.450
What finally squeezes it out as rain?

9
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.010
In this mission, you'll find the moment
when invisible vapour turns into cloud

10
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.230
droplets.

11
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.750
Then you'll compare three
very different skies,

12
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.430
and find what they have in common.

13
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:44.120
Your mission: find out what turns
invisible water vapour into rain.
